id: pm-hb7ug8
title: "One declared output-bounding dimension set on every read surface: 18 flag spellings across 19 commands collapse to include / how-much / cost / encoding, with a precedence algebra and permanent aliases"
description: "Consolidate every way to ask a pm read for less output into one dimension set available identically on all read surfaces, with declared composition precedence and zero removed spellings."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: agent-ergonomics,cli-grammar,contracts,pm-cli,simplification,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:07:31.733Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T07:02:32.347Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 960
acceptance_criteria: "One declared bounding dimension set (include, how much, cost, encoding) is available identically on every read surface, or the contract states per surface why a dimension is inapplicable; Pairwise availability disagreement between any two read surfaces over the dimension set is zero, asserted by a contract test rather than reviewed; No read surface supports zero bounding dimensions; files, docs, stats and aggregate gain the set; A declared precedence algebra states which dimension wins when two are supplied, and get --depth deep --for inspect has a contract-defined result; Every one of the 18 current spellings continues to work as a hidden alias with a one-line migration hint; no invocation in any recorded transcript breaks; A gate fails when a new read command or a new bounding flag is added outside the declared set, so the growth trend stops rather than being periodically re-measured"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Deliver a universal, fully-customizable PM tool whose baseline primitives (via the pm SDK) adapt to any project"
value: "Turns asking for less output from a per-command availability matrix into one learnable contract, which is the token cost every agent pays on every invocation."
outcome: An agent learns one bounding vocabulary once and applies it to every read surface in the product.
why_now: Two recorded simplification axes independently conclude that noun consolidation is a null move until output bounding is uniform; this is the smallest tranche and the one an agent pays for on every call.
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: high
